THIS IS NOT OPEN SOURCE.

The repository is public so that anyone can inspect how the application is
built and download official releases. Public visibility does NOT grant any
right to use the code.

PERMITTED
1. Using the PsyGames application itself. It is free at launch.
2. Reading and studying the source code.
3. Downloading official builds from Releases and installing them for
   personal use.
4. Submitting bug reports and suggestions.

PROHIBITED WITHOUT WRITTEN PERMISSION FROM THE COPYRIGHT HOLDER
1. Copying, porting or reusing the code, in whole or in part, in any product
   of your own — commercial or non-commercial.
2. Modifying the code and distributing modified versions.
3. Creating derivative products, including builds under a different name
   or different branding.
4. Publishing the application or any part of it to app stores, catalogues
   or third-party platforms.
5. Selling, renting or providing it as a service.
6. Using the application's materials — task texts, stimulus sets,
   translations, images, sounds — separately from the application.

ON THE COMMERCIAL FUTURE
Being free at launch is a stage, not a property of the product. The roadmap
includes paid capabilities. All commercial rights remain with the copyright
holder, and the free period does not limit them in any way.

THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS
The application uses libraries under their own licenses (see package.json and
Cargo.toml). This license covers only PsyGames' own code and materials, not
third-party components, which carry their own terms.

NO WARRANTY
The software is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind. PsyGames is a
training tool, not a medical device: it does not diagnose and does not replace
consulting a doctor. The copyright holder is not liable for any damages arising
from use of the software.

LICENSING
If you want to use the code or the materials, arrange it in writing. Enquiries
via the Issues section of this repository.
